=begin

    Dramatically shortens combat text. Each round of someone's combat (an attack or spell, every
    roll, hit, crit and status line after it, up to the next prompt) becomes a short summary. By
    default your own combat, and anything aimed at you, is left alone.

    Combat is recognized with Lich's own GemStone combat definitions (the ones the combat tracker
    uses), and kills and creature status come from the game's own creature data, so the script
    keeps up with Lich instead of carrying its own message lists.

    USAGE:
        ;briefcombat                        - start, using previous settings

    OPTIONAL PARAMETERS:
        -x, --extreme                       - extreme mode: one line per round (saved)
        --no-extreme                        - standard mode: damage, crits and status per creature (saved)
        all, --all                          - also shorten your own combat (saved)
        --no-all                            - leave your own combat alone (saved, default)
        --exclude=<players>                 - never shorten these players' combat, comma or space separated (saved)
        --numbers / --no-numbers            - show / hide roll lines (AS/DS, CS/TD, SMR) (saved, default on)
        --flares / --no-flares              - show / hide flare lines (** ... **) (saved, default on)
        --creatures / --no-creatures        - also shorten creatures' attacks on other players (saved, default off)
        --you / --no-you                    - also shorten attacks on you and what happens to you (saved, default off)
        everything                          - shorten everything possible: same as all --you --creatures (saved)

        --debug                             - echo why each round was or wasn't shortened, this run only
        --help                              - show this help and exit
        --list                              - show current settings and exit

    Unless you use --you, attacks on you and lines about you (stuns, falls, dodges) are never
    hidden. Awards, found silver and your own death are always shown.

        author: Daedeus
  contributors: Tysong, Ragz, Gemini AI
          game: Gemstone
          name: briefcombat
          tags: brief, briefcombat, condensing, condense, combat, squelch
      required: Lich >= 5.25.0
       version: 2.0.0

    changelog:
      2.0.0 (2026-11-25)
        - Rewritten on Lich's own combat definitions and creature data: recognizes far more combat
          (maneuvers, spells, bleeds) and names the spell that was cast
        - Your own spells' effects, including later cycles, are no longer shortened unless you use "all"
        - Attacks on you and lines about you (like being stunned) are never hidden, and show right
          away instead of waiting for the summary
        - Two players acting in the same moment now get separate summaries
        - Other players' bleeding is now shortened too
        - New --creatures option to also shorten creatures' attacks on other players
        - New --you option, and "everything", to also shorten attacks on you and what happens to you,
          including creature attacks Lich doesn't recognize yet
        - Kills come from the game's creature data instead of guessing from death messages
        - No more blank line after each summary
        - --exclude now matches whole player names only ("Bob" no longer also leaves "Bobbington" alone)
        - Fix the Wrayth/StormFront compass sometimes not updating after a move that has roundtime
        - Fix the Bounties window not updating after a kill that was part of a shortened combat block
        - Fix vitals, experience, roundtime and other panels going stale while combat is shortened
        - Fix arriving in a new room (e.g. a group teleport) right after someone casts hiding the whole room
        - Combat summaries no longer briefly delay all game output
        - Fix shortened spells with no target sometimes showing a blank line instead of what happened
        - Needs Lich 5.25.0 or newer
      1.0.5 (2026-09-17)
        - Fix constant redefinition on subsequent runs
      1.0.4 (2026-08-20)
        - Fix squelched lines silently dropping frontend formatting tags (pushBold/popBold, mono),
          which could leave bold or mono formatting stuck on screen until an unrelated later
          message happened to clear it (rare, frontend-dependent)
        - Fix a related regression from an early version of that same fix: forwarding every
          formatting tag instead of just the net imbalance was producing a blank line for nearly
          every squelched combat message, since most squelch balanced pushBold/popBold in the
          same line
        - Fix multi-part compressed summaries joining with inconsistent line breaks
      1.0.3 (2026-02-02)
        - Added --flares and --no-flares options
        - Added --numbers and -no-numbers options
        - Updated help messaging
        - Fix ball spell detection by moving spell guessing logic before target switch return
        - Fix some punctuation, fixed bugs with message selection
        - fix bounty task kills remaining being hidden
        - catch throwing weapon and volley messaging
      1.0.2 (2026-01-31)
        - Standard mode now keeps numbers and body part damage.
        - Standard mode now separates aoe damage to each target affected.
        - Added recognition for a few more actions
      1.0.1 (2026-01-29)
        - Bugfix in @instance variable location
      1.0.0 (2026-01-25)
        - Refactor into a module instead of using global variables
        - Refactor most regex patterns to the top of the file
        - Start handling sentences of different structure, like ambient (no player noun) or target before verbs
        - Added more abilities to recognize, a handful of WEAPON and SHIELD abilities
        - Fix ignore self, by default will not compress self generated actions, unless the "all" parameter is used
        - Added CharSettings support to remember settings between runs
        - Added --help flag to display usage information
        - Added --list flag to show current settings
        - Added --debug flag to enable debug output
        - Improved parameter parsing with --no-extreme and --no-all options

=end

module BriefCombat
  # Drop constants left by an earlier run this session so a restart loads the
  # current definitions without already-initialized warnings.
  %i[HOOK_NAME HOOK_PRIORITY MIN_LICH LEGACY_HOOK_NAMES GENERIC_ATTACKS].each do |name|
    remove_const(name) if const_defined?(name, false)
  end

  HOOK_NAME = 'briefcombat'
  # Higher runs first. Above the default (0), so briefcombat sees each line as
  # the game sent it; combatstream (-1000) runs after it and gets the summaries.
  HOOK_PRIORITY = 50
  MIN_LICH = '5.25.0'
  # The 1.x hook name, removed at start in case an old copy is still hooked.
  LEGACY_HOOK_NAMES = %w[brief2].freeze

  # parse_attack names that say nothing more than the opening line already
  # does; anything else (:earthen_fury, :bane ...) names the spell or ability.
  GENERIC_ATTACKS = %i[attack cast uac fire throw bleed poison_tick].freeze

  # Settings, saved per character under CharSettings['briefcombat'] with the
  # same keys 1.x used, so existing settings carry over.
  class Settings
    %i[KEY DEFAULTS FLAGS EVERYTHING].each { |name| remove_const(name) if const_defined?(name, false) }

    KEY = 'briefcombat'
    DEFAULTS = {
      'extreme_mode'     => false,
      'compress_self'    => false,
      'show_numbers'     => true,
      'show_flares'      => true,
      'creature_attacks' => false,
      'compress_you'     => false,
      'excluded_players' => []
    }.freeze
    FLAGS = {
      '-x' => ['extreme_mode', true], '--extreme' => ['extreme_mode', true], '--no-extreme' => ['extreme_mode', false],
      'all' => ['compress_self', true], '--all' => ['compress_self', true], '--no-all' => ['compress_self', false],
      '--numbers' => ['show_numbers', true], '--no-numbers' => ['show_numbers', false],
      '--flares' => ['show_flares', true], '--no-flares' => ['show_flares', false],
      '--creatures' => ['creature_attacks', true], '--no-creatures' => ['creature_attacks', false],
      '--you' => ['compress_you', true], '--no-you' => ['compress_you', false]
    }.freeze
    # "everything": shorten all combat, yours and what happens to you included
    EVERYTHING = %w[compress_self compress_you creature_attacks].freeze

    attr_reader :values

    # @param args [Array<String>] the script's arguments
    # @param line [String] the full argument line (for quoted --exclude lists)
    # @param store [Hash] CharSettings (or a Hash in specs)
    def initialize(args, line, store)
      saved = store[KEY].is_a?(Hash) ? store[KEY] : {}
      @values = DEFAULTS.merge(saved.compact)
      args.each do |arg|
        EVERYTHING.each { |key| @values[key] = true } if %w[everything --everything].include?(arg)
        key, value = FLAGS[arg]
        @values[key] = value if key
      end
      if line =~ /--exclude=(["']?)(.+?)\1(?:\s+|$)/
        @values['excluded_players'] = Regexp.last_match(2).split(/[\s,]+/)
      end
      @debug = args.include?('--debug') || args.include?('-d')
      store[KEY] = @values
    end

    def extreme? = @values['extreme_mode'] == true
    def numbers? = @values['show_numbers'] != false
    def flares? = @values['show_flares'] != false
    def creature_attacks? = @values['creature_attacks'] == true
    def compress_you? = @values['compress_you'] == true
    def debug? = @debug

    # 1.x let "you"/"self" in the exclude list mean "leave my combat alone".
    def compress_self?
      @values['compress_self'] == true && excluded_names.none? { |name| %w[you self].include?(name.downcase) }
    end

    # @return [Array<String>] player names whose combat is never shortened
    def excluded
      excluded_names.reject { |name| %w[you self].include?(name.downcase) }
    end

    def excluded_names = Array(@values['excluded_players']).map(&:to_s).reject(&:empty?)
  end

  # Recognizes combat with lich-5's GemStone combat definitions, plus the few
  # openers they don't cover. Built from whatever the running Lich provides,
  # so a family a release lacks is skipped rather than failing.
  class Classifier
    %i[CREATURE_LINK PLAYER_LINK ACTOR OPENERS ROLL_TEXT BOUNTY DEATH ATTACK_HINT DAMAGE_TEXT PREP STATUS_TEXT AIMED_AT_YOU OUTCOME].each do |name|
      remove_const(name) if const_defined?(name, false)
    end

    # A MonsterBold creature: "<pushBold/>a <a exist="123" ...>name</a><popBold/>"
    CREATURE_LINK = %r{<pushBold/>(?<article>(?:[Aa]n?|[Tt]he|[Ss]ome) )?<a exist="(?<id>\d+)" noun="(?<noun>[^"]+)">(?<name>[^<]+)</a><popBold/>}
    PLAYER_LINK = /<a exist="-\d+" noun="[^"]+">[^<]+<\/a>/
    ACTOR = /\A\s*(?<actor>#{PLAYER_LINK}|You\b)/

    # Openers parse_attack doesn't recognize (measured on 2.2M lines of GS4
    # logs against lich-5 5.25.0): spell preparation and a few maneuvers.
    # Each opens a round for the actor at the start of the line.
    OPENERS = [
      /\A\s*(?:#{PLAYER_LINK}|You) gestures?\./,
      /chants? a reverent litany/,
      /skillfully begins? to weave another verse into/,
      /draws? an intricately glowing pattern in the air before/,
      /\bwaves? (?:your|an?) .+? (?:at|over) /,
      /\bcharges? forward at .+? attempts? a shield charge/,
      /\btakes? a menacing step toward/,
      /\bsnaps? (?:your|his|her) arm forward, (?:throwing|hurling)/,
      /\blooses? arrow after arrow/,
      /\btakes? quick assessment and raises?/,
      /An ominous shadow falls over your surroundings/,
      /erupts from your crackling aura, lashing towards/
    ].freeze

    # parse_attack costs 80-120us a line, too much for every line on the
    # game thread. In 2.2M lines of GS4 logs, all but a handful of the
    # attacks it matched name a creature (MonsterBold) or hold one of these
    # words; this gate sends it about 10% of lines.
    ATTACK_HINT = Regexp.union(
      %r{<pushBold/>[^<]*<a exist="\d}, /blood|bleed/i, /gesture|channels? at|palette|whip of energy/,
      /explodes from the ground|rolls into the area|earth cracks beneath|stalagmites burst|hailstones pound/,
      /sandstorm swirls|flaming rocks|Waves of sacred energy|flame flare up around|snowflakes settle/,
      /stomp your foot|lash out again and again|in a wide arc/
    )

    # The common damage wordings, matched before lich's Damage family (which
    # costs ~200-350us a line): "... and hit for 20 points of damage!",
    # "... 15 points of damage!", "searing it for 30 points of damage!",
    # "suffers an additional 2 damage!". Damage only runs on the rest, and
    # only when a number comes right before "damage".
    DAMAGE_TEXT = /(?:\.\.\. |\bfor |additional )(?:and hits? for )?(\d+) (?:points? of )?damage!/

    # A creature (or trap) line aimed at you. Lich's definitions miss many
    # creature-specific attacks ("attempts to pincer you!"), and this also
    # matches flavor ("looks at you in utter terror!"), so a round it opens
    # is provisional: see Round#fought?.
    AIMED_AT_YOU = /\b(?:at|toward|towards|into) you\b|\battempts? to \w+ you\b|\bengages you\b/
    # How an attack ended, when there is no roll or damage line.
    OUTCOME = /\bmiss(?:es)?\b|\bevade|\bblock|\bparr(?:y|ies)|\bdodge|\bdeflect|harmlessly/i

    # Opening lines that only say a spell is coming; the actor's next action
    # line ("hurls a seething blast of steam at ...") makes a better header.
    PREP = /gestures?\b|chants? a reverent litany|weave another verse|draws? an intricately glowing pattern/

    # Roll lines, for Lich builds whose Resolutions family misses one.
    ROLL_TEXT = /\b(?:AS|CS|UAF|d100)\b.*[=:]|\[SMR result/
    BOUNTY = /You succeeded in your task|kills? remaining\.\]/

    # Status wordings from 1.x, for lines Lich's Statuses family misses
    # (e.g. "loses her balance and falls over!" on 5.25).
    STATUS_TEXT = {
      'knocked down' => /falls over|(?:dragged|knocked|flattening itself) (?:down |to the (?:ground|floor))|collapses on/,
      'frozen'       => /freezes in place|encased in a thick block of ice|stops all movement/,
      'webbed'       => /ensnared in thick strands of webbing/,
      'sympathized'  => /eyes begin to glow (?:purple|dark)/,
      'pinned'       => /\bpins? .* to the/,
      'buffeted'     => /buffeted by/
    }.freeze

    # Death text, for creatures without crtrStatus data (older servers).
    # (1.x wrote this with /x, which drops the spaces, so it never matched.)
    DEATH = Regexp.union(
      /tries to crawl away on the (?:ground|floor) but/, /rolls over on the (?:ground|floor) and goes still/,
      /consumed by ethereal flame/, /(?:collapses|crashes) to the (?:ground|floor)/, /falls to the (?:ground|floor) motionless/,
      /lets out a ragged gasp before collapsing/, /goes still/, /lets out a final/, /\bdies\b/
    )

    def initialize(gemstone = Lich::Gemstone)
      defs = gemstone::Combat::Definitions
      @attack = gemstone::Combat::Parser.method(:parse_attack)
      @families = { roll: defs::Resolutions, damage: defs::Damage, flare: defs::Flares, status: defs::Statuses }
                  .transform_values { |family| family.method(:parse) }
      @crits = gemstone::CritRanks.method(:parse)
    end

    # What a line opens, if it starts someone's combat.
    #
    # @param text [String] the line, out-of-band XML already removed
    # @param provisional [Boolean] also offer a provisional attack on you
    #   (only --you summarizes those)
    # @return [Hash, nil] parse_attack's result, or the same shape for an opener
    def opener(text, provisional: false)
      attack = attack(text)
      return attack if attack
      return (provisional ? aimed_at_you(text) : nil) unless OPENERS.any? { |pattern| text.match?(pattern) }

      result = { name: :cast, target: first_creature(text) || {} }
      result[:inbound] = true if text.match?(/\b(?:at|toward|over) you[.!]?\s*\z/)
      actor = text[ACTOR, :actor]
      result[:attacker] = { id: actor[/-\d+/].to_i, name: actor.gsub(/<[^>]+>/, '') } if actor && actor != 'You'
      result
    end

    # @return [Hash, nil] a provisional attack on you, for a creature or trap
    #   line aimed at you that parse_attack doesn't know
    def aimed_at_you(text)
      return nil if text.start_with?(' ') || !text.match?(/<a exist="\d/)

      plain = text.gsub(/<[^>]+>/, '')
      return nil if plain.match?(/\A\s*You\b/) || !plain.match?(AIMED_AT_YOU)

      creature = first_creature(text)
      { name: :attack, target: {}, inbound: true, tentative: true,
        attacker: creature && { id: creature[:id], noun: creature[:noun], name: creature[:name] } }
    end

    # @return [Hash, nil] parse_attack's result, for a line that may hold one.
    #   Indented lines (rolls, damage, crits, statuses) are skipped: 4 of
    #   ~25,000 in the logs were attacks, all flare lines.
    def attack(text)
      return nil if text.start_with?(' ') || !text.match?(ATTACK_HINT)

      safely { @attack.call(text) }
    end

    # Classifies a line inside a round. Each family runs only on lines that
    # can hold it (measured on the logs): damage lines say "damage", crit
    # text is indented or follows a damage line.
    #
    # @param after_damage [Boolean] the previous line was damage
    # @param attack [Hash, false, nil] parse_attack's result if the caller
    #   already has it (false: checked, none), nil to check here
    # @return [Array(Symbol, Object)] [kind, data]; kind :line if nothing matched
    def event(text, after_damage: false, attack: nil)
      return [:bounty, nil] if text.match?(BOUNTY)
      return [:roll, nil] if text.match?(ROLL_TEXT)
      if (damage = text.match(DAMAGE_TEXT))
        return [:damage, { damage: damage[1].to_i }]
      end

      @families.each do |kind, parse|
        next if kind == :damage && !text.match?(/\d (?:points? of )?damage/)

        data = safely { parse.call(text) }
        return [kind, data] if data && data != {} && data != []
      end
      return [:flare, nil] if text.include?('**')

      STATUS_TEXT.each { |status, pattern| return [:status, { status: status, action: :add }] if text.match?(pattern) }

      if after_damage || text.start_with?('  ')
        crit = safely { @crits.call(text) }
        detail = crit.is_a?(Hash) ? crit.values.first : nil
        return [:crit, detail] if detail.is_a?(Hash) && detail[:type] != 'generic'
      end
      attack = attack(text) if attack.nil?
      return [:attack, attack] if attack

      [:line, nil]
    end

    # @return [Hash, nil] {id:, noun:, name:, link:} of the first creature in text
    def first_creature(text)
      match = text.match(CREATURE_LINK)
      match && { id: match[:id].to_i, noun: match[:noun], name: match[:name], link: match[0] }
    end

    # @return [Hash, nil] the first player in text other than the actor (a
    #   blood burst or bleed on a groupmate), as a target
    def first_player(text)
      links = text.scan(%r{<a exist="(-\d+)" noun="([^"]+)">([^<]+)</a>})
      actor = text[ACTOR, :actor]
      id, noun, name = links.find { |(link_id, _, _)| !actor || !actor.include?(%(exist="#{link_id}")) }
      id && { id: id.to_i, noun: noun, name: name.sub(/'s\z/, '') }
    end

    # @return [Hash, nil] the last creature in text (a ricochet's new target)
    def last_creature(text)
      match = text.to_enum(:scan, CREATURE_LINK).map { Regexp.last_match }.last
      match && { id: match[:id].to_i, noun: match[:noun], name: match[:name], link: match[0] }
    end

    def dead_text?(text) = text.match?(DEATH)

    private

    # A definition that raises on an odd line must not end the round.
    def safely
      yield
    rescue StandardError
      nil
    end
  end

  # One round of someone's combat, from its opening line to the next prompt.
  class Round
    %i[Target YOU].each { |name| remove_const(name) if const_defined?(name, false) }

    Target = Struct.new(:id, :noun, :name, :damage, :rolls, :flares, :crits, :statuses, :killed, :message, :you) do
      def active? = damage.positive? || !crits.empty? || !statuses.empty? || killed || !flares.empty?
    end
    YOU = { id: :you, name: 'you' }.freeze

    attr_reader :first, :actor, :key, :spell, :targets, :bounty, :last_line, :action_line, :lines

    # @param text [String] the opening line
    # @param opener [Hash] Classifier#opener's result
    # @param actor [Symbol] :self, :other, :creature or :ambient
    # @param classifier [Classifier]
    def initialize(text, opener, actor, classifier)
      @classifier = classifier
      @first = text.chomp
      @lines = [@first]
      @tentative = opener[:tentative]
      @fought = !@tentative
      @actor = actor
      @key = Round.key(actor, opener)
      @spell = spell_name(opener[:name])
      @targets = {}
      @pending_rolls = []
      @current = nil
      # a creature's attack: its own link is the attacker, never a target
      attacker = opener.dig(:attacker, :id).to_i
      @creature_attacker = attacker if attacker.positive?
      if opener[:inbound]
        switch_to(YOU)
      elsif @creature_attacker
        switch_to(classifier.first_player(text))
      else
        named = classifier.first_creature(text)
        target = opener[:target]
        switch_to(named && target&.dig(:id) && named[:id] != target[:id] ? target : (named || target))
        switch_to(classifier.first_player(text)) unless @current
      end
      @unnamed = opener.dig(:target, :name)
      add_damage(classifier, text)
    end

    # @param text [String] a line inside the round
    # @param attack [Hash, false, nil] the line's parse_attack result, if known
    def add(text, attack: nil)
      line = text.chomp
      @lines << line
      return if line.strip.empty?

      kind, data = @classifier.event(line, after_damage: @after_damage, attack: attack)
      @fought ||= %i[roll damage crit status].include?(kind) || line.match?(Classifier::OUTCOME)
      @after_damage = kind == :damage
      # a line about you ("You are stunned ...") is about you, whoever acted
      switch_to(YOU) if %i[status damage crit].include?(kind) && line.match?(/\A\s*(?:<[^>]+>)*You\b/)
      case kind
      when :bounty then @bounty = line
      when :roll then (@current ? @current.rolls << line : @pending_rolls << line)
      when :damage then hit(line)&.then { |target| target.damage += data[:damage].to_i }
      when :flare then (hit(line) || @current)&.flares&.push(line)
      when :crit then (hit(line) || @current)&.crits&.push(line)
      when :status then status(line, data)
      when :attack then attack(line, data)
      else other(line)
      end
      mark_kill(line) if @classifier.dead_text?(line)
    end

    # @return [Array<Target>] the creatures this round touched, in order
    def touched = @targets.values

    # False for a provisional round (a line aimed at you that Lich doesn't
    # know) that never turned into combat: no roll, damage, status or
    # outcome before the prompt. Such a round is sent as it came.
    def fought? = @fought

    # Who acted: rounds by different actors are kept apart.
    def self.key(actor, opener)
      %i[other creature].include?(actor) ? opener.dig(:attacker, :id) : actor
    end

    private

    def hit(line)
      target = target_for(@classifier.first_creature(line)) if line.include?('<pushBold/>')
      # no link at all (MonsterBold off, some ambient spells): one nameless
      # target, so damage and status still count
      target ||= @current || (@current = target_for({ id: 0, name: @unnamed }))
      flush_rolls(target)
      target
    end

    def status(line, data)
      target = data.is_a?(Hash) && data[:target] ? target_for(@classifier.first_creature(data[:target].to_s)) : nil
      target ||= hit(line)
      return unless target

      name = data.is_a?(Hash) ? data[:status] : data
      target.statuses << name.to_s.tr('_', ' ') if name && data.is_a?(Hash) && data[:action] != :remove
    end

    def attack(line, data)
      @spell ||= spell_name(data[:name])
      @action_line ||= line if own_action?(line, data)
      creature = data.dig(:target, :id) ? data[:target] : @classifier.last_creature(line)
      switch_to(creature) if creature
      @current&.message ||= line
    end

    # A line of this round's actor doing something, other than preparing.
    def own_action?(line, data)
      return false if line.match?(Classifier::PREP)

      @actor == :self ? line.match?(/\A\s*You\b/) : data.dig(:attacker, :id) == @key
    end

    def other(line)
      creature = @classifier.last_creature(line)
      if creature
        switch_to(creature)
        @current.message = line
      else
        @last_line = line
      end
    end

    def add_damage(classifier, text)
      kind, data = classifier.event(text.chomp)
      hit(text).damage += data[:damage].to_i if kind == :damage
    end

    def mark_kill(line)
      target = target_for(@classifier.first_creature(line)) || @current
      target.killed = true if target
    end

    def switch_to(creature)
      target = target_for(creature)
      return unless target

      @current = target
      flush_rolls(@current)
    end

    def target_for(creature)
      return nil unless creature && creature[:id]
      return nil if creature[:id] == @creature_attacker

      @targets[creature[:id]] ||= Target.new(creature[:id], creature[:noun], creature[:name], 0, [], [], [], [], false, nil,
                                             creature[:id] == :you)
    end

    def flush_rolls(target)
      return unless target && !@pending_rolls.empty?

      target.rolls.concat(@pending_rolls)
      @pending_rolls.clear
    end

    def spell_name(name)
      return nil if name.nil? || GENERIC_ATTACKS.include?(name)

      name.to_s.split('_').map(&:capitalize).join(' ')
    end
  end

  # Turns a finished round into the lines the player sees.
  class Renderer
    # @param settings [Settings]
    # @param dead [#call] creature id -> true if the game says it is dead
    def initialize(settings, dead)
      @settings = settings
      @dead = dead
    end

    # @param round [Round]
    # @param closing [String, nil] the prompt line that ended the round
    # @return [String] newline-terminated client text
    def render(round, closing)
      return "#{[*round.lines, closing&.chomp].compact.join("\r\n")}\r\n" unless round.fought?

      targets = round.touched
      targets.each { |target| target.killed ||= @dead.call(target.id) if target.id.is_a?(Integer) && target.id.positive? }
      lines = [header(round, targets)]
      lines.concat(@settings.extreme? ? extreme(targets) : standard(targets, round.first))
      lines << round.last_line if targets.none?(&:active?) && round.last_line
      lines << round.bounty if round.bounty
      lines << closing.chomp if closing
      "#{lines.compact.join("\r\n")}\r\n"
    end

    private

    def header(round, targets)
      line = (round.first.match?(Classifier::PREP) && round.action_line || round.first).dup
      if round.spell && line == round.first
        line.sub!(/\b(?:You gesture)\b/, "You cast #{round.spell}") ||
          line.sub!(/\bgestures\b/, "casts #{round.spell}") ||
          line.sub!(/chants a reverent litany.*/, "chants #{round.spell}.") ||
          line.sub!(/skillfully begins to weave another verse into .*/, "weaves #{round.spell}.")
      end
      count = targets.count { |target| !target.you }
      return line if count < 2

      "#{line.sub(/[.!]+\s*\z/, '')} and #{count == 2 ? '1 other' : "#{count - 1} others"}."
    end

    def standard(targets, first)
      targets.flat_map do |target|
        lines = []
        lines.concat(target.rolls) if @settings.numbers?
        lines.concat(target.flares) if @settings.flares?
        crits = target.crits.uniq.map(&:strip)
        if target.damage.positive?
          lines << "  .. #{target.damage} damage!#{"  #{crits.shift}" if crits.any?}"
        elsif crits.empty? && target.message && target.message != first
          # no damage: show what happened to it instead, as 1.x did
          lines << target.message.strip
        end
        lines.concat(crits.map { |crit| "   #{crit}" })
        if target.killed || !target.statuses.empty?
          lines << "  #{display_name(target)} #{target.you ? 'are' : 'is'} #{status_text(target)}!"
        end
        lines
      end
    end

    def extreme(targets)
      you, targets = targets.partition(&:you)
      counts = Hash.new(0)
      targets.each do |target|
        next counts['killed'] += 1 if target.killed

        target.statuses.uniq.each { |status| counts[status] += 1 }
      end
      damage = targets.sum(&:damage)
      parts = []
      parts << "#{counts.delete('killed')} targets <pushBold/>KILLED<popBold/>" if counts['killed'].positive?
      counts.each { |status, n| parts << "#{n} #{n == 1 ? 'target' : 'targets'} #{status}" }
      parts << "#{damage} damage dealt" if damage.positive?
      lines = parts.empty? ? [] : ["  ... #{parts.join(', ')}!"]
      you.each do |target|
        mine = target.statuses.uniq
        mine << "#{target.damage} damage taken" if target.damage.positive?
        lines << "  ... you: #{mine.join(', ')}!" unless mine.empty?
      end
      lines
    end

    def status_text(target)
      target.killed ? '<pushBold/>KILLED<popBold/>' : target.statuses.uniq.join(', ')
    end

    def display_name(target)
      return 'You' if target.you
      return "<a exist=\"#{target.id}\" noun=\"#{target.noun}\">#{target.name}</a>" if target.id.negative?
      return target.name ? "The #{target.name}" : 'It' if target.id.zero?

      prefix = target.name.to_s.match?(/\A[aeiou]/i) ? 'An' : 'A'
      "<pushBold/>#{prefix} <a exist=\"#{target.id}\" noun=\"#{target.noun}\">#{target.name}</a><popBold/>"
    end
  end

  # Decides, line by line, what to shorten. Sees only story text: the Client
  # below has already set aside XML meant for panels and side windows.
  class Engine
    %i[SIMPLE_SQUELCH SELF_SPELL_PREP SELF_SPELL_XML SELF_SEARCH OTHER_SEARCH ABOUT_YOU YOUR_STATE ALWAYS_SHOW].each do |name|
      remove_const(name) if const_defined?(name, false)
    end

    # Lines nobody needs to see while this script runs.
    SIMPLE_SQUELCH = [
      /Roundtime:/,
      /incandescent veil fades/,                            # 1608
      /knobby layer of bark/,                               # 605
      /briefly before decaying into dust\./,                # 709 decay
      /In a breathtaking display of ability and combat mastery|spins about looking mighty stirred up|looks determined and focused/, # mstrike prep
      /removes a single(.*)from/,                           # get arrow
      /\bnocks? an?\b/,                                     # arrow nock (not "knocks a")
      /surge of empowerment/
    ].freeze
    # Your own spell preparation, hidden with "all".
    SELF_SPELL_PREP = /Your spell(?:song)? is ready\.|You gesture\.|Cast Roundtime \d Seconds?\.?/
    SELF_SPELL_XML = /<castTime value='\d+'\/>|<spell exist='spell'>/
    SELF_SEARCH = %r{You search the <pushBold/>|<pushBold/>.*<popBold/> (?:had nothing of interest|didn't carry any silver|had nothing else of value)}
    OTHER_SEARCH = %r{<a exist="-\d+" noun="\w+">\w+</a> searches <pushBold/>.*<popBold/>}
    # Shown in every mode, --you included: awards, loot, your own death.
    ALWAYS_SHOW = /\AYou have been awarded|\bdiscover \d+ silvers?\b|\AYou (?:are|have been) (?:now )?(?:dead|slain)|\AYou have died/
    # A change to your own state (stunned, a spell landing, an award): shown
    # even inside your own round with "all".
    YOUR_STATE = /\A\s*You (?:are|have been)\b|\AYou .*\bdiscover \d+ silvers?\b/
    # Lines about you: shown even inside someone else's round (a spell landing
    # on you, a stun, a dodge, your own gear reacting), except a creature's
    # death flavor, which only starts with "You hear".
    ABOUT_YOU = /\A\s*(?:You(?! hear a sound like)|Your)\b|\b(?:at|toward|towards) you[!.]\z|\byour (?:head|neck|chest|back|abdomen|arm|leg|hand|eye)/

    attr_reader :round

    # @param settings [Settings]
    # @param classifier [Classifier]
    # @param dead [#call] creature id -> dead?
    # @param log [#call, nil] debug output
    def initialize(settings, classifier, dead: ->(_id) { false }, log: nil)
      @settings = settings
      @classifier = classifier
      @renderer = Renderer.new(settings, dead)
      @log = log
      # who an actor-less effect (an Earthen Fury cycle ...) last belonged to,
      # by attack name: later cycles arrive with nobody named
      @effect_owner = {}
      reset!
    end

    def reset!
      @round = nil
      @search = false
      @last_actor = nil
    end

    # True while a round or a shortened search is open.
    def busy? = !@round.nil? || @search

    # Ends an open round early (a room change): the summary, or nil.
    def interrupt
      summary = @round && @renderer.render(@round, nil)
      reset!
      summary
    end

    # Whether a line would be squelched outright (used for side-window lines).
    def squelched?(text) = SIMPLE_SQUELCH.any? { |pattern| text.match?(pattern) }

    # @param text [String] story text, out-of-band XML removed
    # @param raw [String] the full chunk (for XML-only clues like castTime)
    # @return [String, nil] text itself to send it unchanged, a replacement, or nil
    def process(text, raw = text)
      prompt = text.include?('<prompt')
      return search_line(text, prompt) if @search
      return round_line(text, prompt) if @round

      if prompt
        @last_actor = nil
        return text
      end
      return text if excluded?(text)
      return nil if squelched?(text)

      if (opener = @classifier.opener(text, provisional: @settings.compress_you?))
        return open_round(text, opener)
      end

      return text if plain(text).match?(@settings.compress_you? ? ALWAYS_SHOW : YOUR_STATE)
      return nil if @settings.compress_self? && (raw.match?(SELF_SPELL_XML) || text.match?(SELF_SPELL_PREP))
      return nil if text.match?(SELF_SEARCH)

      if text.match?(OTHER_SEARCH)
        @search = true
        return @settings.extreme? ? nil : text
      end
      text
    end

    private

    # While another player's search is shortened, everything up to the
    # prompt is its result, except lines about you and attacks on you. An
    # attack on you ends the search, as it ends a round, so its roll and
    # damage lines (which don't start with "You") show too.
    def search_line(text, prompt)
      if prompt
        @search = false
        return text
      end
      return text if plain(text).match?(ALWAYS_SHOW)
      return nil if @settings.compress_you?

      if @classifier.opener(text)&.dig(:inbound) || @classifier.aimed_at_you(text)
        @search = false
        return text
      end
      plain(text).match?(ABOUT_YOU) ? text : nil
    end

    def round_line(text, prompt)
      if prompt
        summary = @renderer.render(@round, text)
        reset!
        return summary
      end

      opener = @classifier.opener(text, provisional: @settings.compress_you?)
      # Without --you, an attack on you ends the open round: otherwise its
      # roll and damage lines (which don't start with "You") fold into the
      # round and are credited to whoever acted. That includes a creature
      # line aimed at you that Lich doesn't recognize, except in your own
      # round, where such a line is usually your own effect ("X looks at you
      # in utter terror!" after your cry).
      unless @settings.compress_you?
        aimed = opener&.dig(:inbound) ? opener : (@round.actor != :self && @classifier.aimed_at_you(text))
        return next_round(text, aimed) if aimed
      end
      if opener && (!opener[:inbound] || @settings.compress_you?) && new_actor?(text, opener)
        # someone else starts acting: this round is over, theirs begins
        return next_round(text, opener)
      end
      line = plain(text)
      return text if line.match?(ALWAYS_SHOW)
      unless @settings.compress_you?
        return text if line.match?(YOUR_STATE)
        return text if @round.actor != :self && (opener&.dig(:inbound) || line.match?(ABOUT_YOU))
      end

      @round.add(text, attack: opener || false)
      nil
    end

    # A line with a named attacker other than this round's, or your own line
    # in someone else's round. An effect with no actor (Fiery debris ...)
    # belongs to the round it shows up in.
    def new_actor?(text, opener)
      actor = actor_of(text, opener)
      return @round.actor != :self if actor == :self
      return false unless opener.dig(:attacker, :id)

      Round.key(actor, opener) != @round.key
    end

    def next_round(text, opener)
      summary = @renderer.render(@round, nil)
      @round = nil
      kept = open_round(text, opener)
      kept ? "#{summary}#{kept}" : summary
    end

    def open_round(text, opener)
      actor = actor_of(text, opener)
      @last_actor = actor if %i[self other].include?(actor)
      if (reason = keep_reason(text, opener, actor))
        debug("kept (#{reason}): #{text}")
        return text
      end
      debug("round (#{actor}, #{opener[:name]}): #{text}")
      @round = Round.new(text, opener, actor, @classifier)
      nil
    end

    # Who a round belongs to.
    #
    # @return [Symbol] :self, :other (a player), :creature, or :ambient
    def actor_of(text, opener)
      attacker = opener[:attacker]
      return attacker[:id].to_i.negative? ? :other : :creature if attacker&.dig(:id)
      return :self if text.match?(/\A\s*(?:You|Your)\b/)
      # a groupmate's bleed names the player; Lich also flags a target it
      # couldn't link (MonsterBold off) as foreign, which is not that
      return :ambient if opener[:foreign_target] && text.match?(Classifier::PLAYER_LINK)

      # An effect with no actor (Fiery debris explodes beneath ...) belongs to
      # whoever acted last before this prompt, and its later cycles to them.
      # Keyed by spell AND target, so a second caster of the same lasting
      # spell on another creature doesn't take over your cycles; the spell
      # alone is the fallback for a cycle that hops to a new target.
      name = opener[:name]
      target = opener.dig(:target, :id) || opener[:target_name] || @classifier.first_creature(text)&.dig(:id)
      if @last_actor
        if name
          @effect_owner[[name, target]] = @last_actor if target
          @effect_owner[name] = @last_actor
        end
        return @last_actor
      end
      (target && @effect_owner[[name, target]]) || @effect_owner[name] || :ambient
    end

    # @return [String, nil] why this round is left alone, or nil to shorten it
    def keep_reason(text, opener, actor)
      return 'excluded player' if excluded?(text)
      return (@settings.compress_you? ? nil : 'aimed at you') if opener[:inbound]
      return 'your own combat' if actor == :self && !@settings.compress_self?
      return 'creature attack' if actor == :creature && !@settings.creature_attacks?

      nil
    end

    # The line as the player reads it: tags removed, no line break.
    def plain(text) = text.gsub(/<[^>]+>/, '').chomp

    # Whole names only: excluding "Bob" must not leave "Bobbington" alone.
    def excluded?(text)
      names = @settings.excluded
      !names.empty? && names.any? { |name| text.match?(/(?<![A-Za-z])#{Regexp.escape(name)}(?![A-Za-z])/) }
    end

    def debug(message)
      @log&.call(message.gsub(/<[^>]+>/, '').strip)
    end
  end

  # Keeps the client's state intact around whatever the Engine hides.
  #
  # The DownstreamHook gets each raw chunk from the game, and returning nil
  # drops all of it. But the server glues XML the client needs onto the same
  # lines as combat text: the compass, vitals and experience panels, the
  # roundtime bar, room panels, side windows such as Bounties. So each chunk
  # is split first:
  #
  # - Out-of-band XML is removed before the Engine sees the line. If the line
  #   goes out unchanged, so does its XML; if the line is hidden or folded
  #   into a summary, the XML is carried onto the next line sent (carrying
  #   it, rather than sending it alone, avoids a blank line in the client).
  # - Formatting state tags (bold, mono) in hidden text are carried the same
  #   way, but only their net imbalance (nearly every combat line holds a
  #   balanced MonsterBold pair). Losing an unbalanced one leaves bold or
  #   mono stuck on (https://github.com/elanthia-online/lich-5/pull/1530).
  # - A line with no story text at all goes out as is, in place.
  # - Side-window lines are never folded into an open round.
  # - A room change ends an open round; the room line is held one chunk so it
  #   starts that chunk, where Lich decorates room titles.
  class Client
    %i[STATE_TAG_PAIRS MONO_ON MONO_OFF COMPASS OUT_OF_BAND TAG SIDE_STREAM SIDE_STREAM_MAX_LINES COMBAT_TEXT
       ROOM_CHANGE CARRY_UNSAFE_START].each do |name|
      remove_const(name) if const_defined?(name, false)
    end

    STATE_TAG_PAIRS = [[/<pushBold\/>/, /<popBold\/>/, '<pushBold/>', '<popBold/>']].freeze
    MONO_ON = /<output class="mono"\s*\/>/
    MONO_OFF = /<output class=""\s*\/>/
    COMPASS = /<compass>.*?<\/compass>/m
    # XML the client shows outside the story window, or uses as its own state.
    OUT_OF_BAND = %r{
      <(?<block>dialogData|component|compass|left|right|spell|openDialog|inv)\b[^>]*(?<!/)>.*?</\k<block>>
      | <(?:dialogData|component|left|right|spell|nav|streamWindow|clearStream|indicator|roundTime|castTime|
           crtrStatus|resource|closeDialog|openDialog|switchQuickBar|exposeContainer|container|clearContainer|
           deleteContainer|image|pushStream|popStream)\b[^>]*/>
    }xm
    TAG = /<[^>]*>/
    # Like Lich's own parser, a push switches windows and a pop switches back.
    SIDE_STREAM = /<(pushStream|popStream)\b/
    # The server often opens a side window and never closes it (most inv and
    # bounty updates), so side-window mode also ends at a prompt or after
    # this many lines.
    SIDE_STREAM_MAX_LINES = 200
    # Because those streams are often left open, only the push line and the
    # one line after it (the shape of a Bounties update) count as window
    # content during a round, and never a line with a creature or a roll.
    COMBAT_TEXT = %r{<pushBold/>|\b(?:AS|CS|UAF|d100)\b|points? of damage}
    ROOM_CHANGE = /<nav\b|<style id=["']roomName["']/
    # Line starts Lich rewrites only at the start of a line: the room title
    # (map id / uid decoration) and the room subtitle (Genie/Frostbite).
    # Carried XML is never put in front of these.
    CARRY_UNSAFE_START = %r{\A(?:<pushStream id="familiar"[^>]*/>)?(?:<resource picture="\d+"/>|<popBold/>)?(?:<style id="roomName"\s*/>|<room>)|\A<streamWindow\b}

    # @param engine [Engine]
    def initialize(engine)
      @engine = engine
      @carry = +''
      @in_side_stream = false
      @side_stream_lines = 0
      @held_room_line = nil
    end

    # The DownstreamHook body.
    #
    # @param line [String, nil] one raw chunk from the game
    # @return [String, nil] what the client gets, or nil
    def call(line)
      return line if line.nil?
      return send_held_room_line(line) if @held_room_line

      side_stream = side_stream_line?(line)
      return line if side_stream && @engine.busy? && side_window_content?(line)

      out_of_band = +''
      text = line.gsub(OUT_OF_BAND) { |xml| out_of_band << xml; '' }

      if @engine.busy? && line.match?(ROOM_CHANGE)
        summary = @engine.interrupt
        return with_carry(line) unless summary

        @held_room_line = line
        return with_carry(summary)
      end
      return with_carry(line) if line.include?('<') && text.gsub(TAG, '').strip.empty?

      result = @engine.process(text, line)
      if result.nil?
        carry("#{out_of_band}#{state_tag_imbalance(text)}")
        return nil
      end
      with_carry(result.equal?(text) ? line : "#{out_of_band}#{result}")
    end

    private

    def send_held_room_line(line)
      held = @held_room_line
      @held_room_line = nil
      result = call(line)
      result.nil? ? held : "#{held}#{result}"
    end

    def side_stream_line?(line)
      side = @in_side_stream
      if line.match?(SIDE_STREAM)
        side = true
        line.scan(SIDE_STREAM) { |(tag)| @in_side_stream = (tag == 'pushStream') }
        @side_stream_lines = 0
      else
        @side_stream_lines += 1
      end
      if line.include?('<prompt') || @side_stream_lines > SIDE_STREAM_MAX_LINES
        @in_side_stream = false
        @side_stream_lines = 0
      end
      side
    end

    def side_window_content?(line)
      return false if line.include?('<prompt') || line.match?(COMBAT_TEXT) || @engine.squelched?(line)

      line.match?(SIDE_STREAM) || @side_stream_lines <= 1
    end

    # Holds XML from a hidden line for the next line sent; only the newest
    # compass is kept.
    def carry(xml)
      return if xml.empty?

      @carry = @carry.gsub(COMPASS, '') if xml.match?(COMPASS)
      @carry += xml
    end

    def with_carry(line)
      return line if @carry.empty? || line.match?(CARRY_UNSAFE_START)

      carried = line.match?(COMPASS) ? @carry.gsub(COMPASS, '') : @carry
      @carry = +''
      "#{carried}#{line}"
    end

    def state_tag_imbalance(text)
      parts = STATE_TAG_PAIRS.map do |open_pattern, close_pattern, open_text, close_text|
        net = text.scan(open_pattern).length - text.scan(close_pattern).length
        net.positive? ? open_text * net : close_text * -net
      end
      mono = text.scan(MONO_ON).length - text.scan(MONO_OFF).length
      parts << (mono.positive? ? '<output class="mono"/>' * mono : '<output class=""/>' * -mono)
      parts.join
    end
  end

  # @return [Boolean] true if the game says creature id is dead (crtrStatus,
  #   kept by Lich's creature registry; GameObj for servers without it)
  def self.dead?(id)
    return true if Lich::Gemstone::Creature[id]&.dead?

    GameObj[id.to_s]&.status.to_s.include?('dead')
  end

  # @return [Boolean] true if this Lich is new enough (pre-releases of later
  #   versions included)
  def self.supported?(version = LICH_VERSION)
    Gem::Version.new(version.to_s) >= Gem::Version.new(MIN_LICH)
  rescue ArgumentError
    false
  end

  def self.say(text)
    defined?(Lich::Messaging) ? Lich::Messaging.msg('info', text) : respond(text)
  end

  def self.show_help
    respond <<~HELP
      briefcombat - shortens combat text into one summary per round

        ;briefcombat                    start, using saved settings
        ;briefcombat -x | --no-extreme  extreme (one line per round) or standard mode
        ;briefcombat all | --no-all     also shorten your own combat, or leave it alone (default)
        ;briefcombat --exclude="A,B"    never shorten these players' combat
        ;briefcombat --no-numbers       hide roll lines (--numbers to show them again)
        ;briefcombat --no-flares        hide flare lines (--flares to show them again)
        ;briefcombat --creatures        also shorten creatures' attacks on other players (--no-creatures)
        ;briefcombat --you              also shorten attacks on you and what happens to you (--no-you)
        ;briefcombat everything         shorten everything possible (all --you --creatures)
        ;briefcombat --debug            echo why each round was or wasn't shortened (this run only)
        ;briefcombat --list             show settings
        ;briefcombat --help             show this help

      Settings are saved per character. Without --you, attacks on you and lines about you are never
      hidden; awards, found silver and your own death always show.
      Extreme mode is recommended for big groups.
    HELP
  end

  def self.show_settings(settings)
    values = settings.values
    respond 'briefcombat settings:'
    respond "  extreme mode:      #{values['extreme_mode']}"
    respond "  shorten own:       #{values['compress_self']}"
    respond "  roll lines:        #{values['show_numbers']}"
    respond "  flare lines:       #{values['show_flares']}"
    respond "  creature attacks:  #{values['creature_attacks']}"
    respond "  about you:         #{values['compress_you']}"
    respond "  excluded players:  #{Array(values['excluded_players']).join(', ')}"
  end

  def self.run(vars)
    args = vars[1..] || []
    return show_help if args.include?('--help') || args.include?('-h')

    unless XMLData.game =~ /^GS/
      echo 'briefcombat is for GemStone IV.'
      return
    end
    unless supported?
      echo "briefcombat needs Lich #{MIN_LICH} or newer (this is #{LICH_VERSION}). Update with: ;lich5-update --update"
      return
    end

    settings = Settings.new(args, vars[0].to_s, CharSettings)
    return show_settings(settings) if args.include?('--list')

    log = settings.debug? ? ->(message) { respond "[briefcombat] #{message}" } : nil
    engine = Engine.new(settings, Classifier.new, dead: method(:dead?), log: log)
    client = Client.new(engine)
    warned = false
    hook = proc do |server_string|
      client.call(server_string)
    rescue StandardError => e
      # DownstreamHook removes a hook that raises: one odd line must not turn
      # the script off for the rest of the session.
      engine.reset!
      unless warned
        warned = true
        Lich.log "briefcombat: #{e.class}: #{e.message}\n\t#{e.backtrace&.first(5)&.join("\n\t")}"
      end
      server_string
    end

    LEGACY_HOOK_NAMES.each { |name| DownstreamHook.remove(name) }
    # persist: false -- Lich removes the hook when the script ends.
    DownstreamHook.add(HOOK_NAME, hook, persist: false, priority: HOOK_PRIORITY)
    # After the hook is in place, and without waiting for the reply: the
    # creature highlighting this script matches on.
    put 'set MonsterBold On'

    mode = settings.extreme? ? 'extreme' : 'standard'
    whose = if settings.compress_you? then "all combat, including what happens to you"
            elsif settings.compress_self? then "everyone's combat"
            else "others' combat (;briefcombat all to include yours)"
            end
    say "briefcombat: #{mode} mode, shortening #{whose}."
    say "briefcombat: leaving #{settings.excluded.join(', ')} alone." unless settings.excluded.empty?
    sleep
  end
end

BriefCombat.run(Script.current.vars)
